    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d205">

                <pb facs="0244" n="238" xml:id="pg238"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">853B.20/50: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Portugal</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Fish</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-04-20T23:00:00-04:00">April 20, 1942—11
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>416. Your 305, April 10, 4 p.m. The Department continues in doubt as to whether
                    the Portuguese Government has taken any steps to correct the situation referred
                    to in this correspondence. It is urgent that this matter be clarified without
                    further delay. You are accordingly requested to obtain from the Foreign Office a
                    definite reply at once, reporting to the Department the precise nature of steps
                    taken.</p>
                <p>It is not clear from your telegram that the Legation is keeping the Consulate in
                    Horta advised of developments, as requested in the Department’s 319, March 31, 9
                    p.m.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
